Capillary recommends using Maven for adding the Capillary SDK to your Android project. Capillary Android SDK is hosted on a GitHub Packages Maven repository.
To add the SDK to your project,Add maven in the repositories section of your project's project/build.gradle file as shown below:repositories {  
   …  
   maven {  
       url "<https://maven.pkg.github.com/Capillary/hydra-sdk-android-maven>"  
       credentials {  
           username props['username']  
           password props['token']  
       }  
   }  
}Create a github.properties file to access the Capillary SDK maven repository.
Use below code snippet:username="USERNAME"
token="TOKEN"Replace USERNAME and TOKEN with your actual credentials.Add the required dependency for your module along with the AndroidX libraries in the app/build.gradle file. The AndroidX libraries make sure that the project has access to the necessary AndroidX components.
Code snippet:dependencies {
    // ...
    implementation("com.capillary:hydra-core:1.9.20")
    implementation("com.capillary:hydra-firebase:1.9.20")
    implementation("com.capillary:hydra-pushbase:1.9.20")
}
